1
00:01:32,780 --> 00:01:35,020
[Forging Justice]

2
00:01:35,220 --> 00:01:37,729
[Episode 7]

3
00:01:38,070 --> 00:01:40,039
This is the fruit we bought for you.

4
00:01:40,280 --> 00:01:41,430
Make sure you eat them

5
00:01:41,430 --> 00:01:42,490
before they go bad,

6
00:01:42,789 --> 00:01:43,200
okay?

7
00:01:43,640 --> 00:01:44,789
And these are toys.

8
00:01:58,509 --> 00:02:00,240
Here, these are some notebooks

9
00:02:00,590 --> 00:02:01,760
and pencils.

10
00:02:01,790 --> 00:02:03,520
You must study hard from now on,

11
00:02:03,560 --> 00:02:04,070
okay?

12
00:02:08,550 --> 00:02:09,460
These are...

13
00:02:10,630 --> 00:02:12,430
clothes we bought for you

14
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:14,060
and your brothers.

15
00:02:14,670 --> 00:02:16,470
You can take turns wearing them.

16
00:02:28,190 --> 00:02:28,520
Here.

17
00:02:28,590 --> 00:02:29,050
This...

18
00:02:29,190 --> 00:02:30,470
Take all of this.

19
00:02:30,680 --> 00:02:32,340
T-This is all the money I have.

20
00:02:32,560 --> 00:02:33,840
Take it all. Take it.

21
00:02:35,030 --> 00:02:35,590
Yingjie.

22
00:02:36,910 --> 00:02:37,370
Take it.

23
00:02:37,710 --> 00:02:38,430
Keep it safe.

24
00:02:38,430 --> 00:02:39,030
Yingjie.

25
00:02:46,910 --> 00:02:47,910
Here, take it.

26
00:02:49,900 --> 00:02:50,960
Our money and Mentor's money

27
00:02:50,960 --> 00:02:51,710
are all here.

28
00:02:51,840 --> 00:02:53,300
That's your pocket money.

29
00:02:53,630 --> 00:02:55,030
This still isn't enough.

30
00:02:55,590 --> 00:02:56,470
Not enough.

31
00:02:57,320 --> 00:02:59,450
How could this little money be enough?

32
00:03:00,800 --> 00:03:01,680
Here's what you do.

33
00:03:01,680 --> 00:03:02,150
You...

34
00:03:02,520 --> 00:03:03,710
Don't give it to your grandma,

35
00:03:03,710 --> 00:03:05,240
and don't carry it with you.

36
00:03:05,310 --> 00:03:07,440
I'll find somewhere to hide it for you.

37
00:03:09,800 --> 00:03:10,240
Here.

38
00:03:11,560 --> 00:03:12,120
It's fine.

39
00:03:12,120 --> 00:03:12,850
No, not here.

40
00:03:13,350 --> 00:03:14,950
You won't be able to reach it.

41
00:03:15,520 --> 00:03:17,920
There's nowhere to hide down there either.

42
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:18,400
You...

43
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:19,530
Yingjie.

44
00:03:19,960 --> 00:03:21,170
This place won't work either.

45
00:03:21,170 --> 00:03:22,240
Don't just stand there.

46
00:03:22,240 --> 00:03:24,120
Hurry up and help me
find a place to hide it.

47
00:03:24,120 --> 00:03:24,800
Help her...

48
00:03:25,390 --> 00:03:25,910
Here.

49
00:03:26,150 --> 00:03:27,800
Here works. This place works.

50
00:03:27,800 --> 00:03:28,400
It's okay.

51
00:03:28,560 --> 00:03:29,300
Come outside with me for a second.

52
00:03:29,300 --> 00:03:30,760
There, under there works.

53
00:03:31,430 --> 00:03:32,800
Don't scare the child.

54
00:03:33,430 --> 00:03:34,000
Yingjie.

55
00:03:34,680 --> 00:03:35,010
No...

56
00:03:35,190 --> 00:03:37,240
H-Help her hide it.

57
00:03:37,500 --> 00:03:38,240
Alright.

58
00:03:38,680 --> 00:03:40,940
Do you think you're redeeming yourself?

59
00:03:47,400 --> 00:03:48,120
Right...

60
00:03:51,800 --> 00:03:53,560
What am I doing?

61
00:03:55,079 --> 00:03:56,560
I understand how you feel.

62
00:03:58,000 --> 00:03:58,710
But if you keep

63
00:03:58,710 --> 00:04:00,640
taking everything upon yourself,

64
00:04:00,840 --> 00:04:01,730
how will you become
a qualified legal professional

65
00:04:01,730 --> 00:04:02,610
in the future?

66
00:04:03,310 --> 00:04:04,560
How long can you keep going?

67
00:04:04,560 --> 00:04:06,160
Have you thought about that?

68
00:04:09,630 --> 00:04:10,160
Alright.

69
00:04:10,280 --> 00:04:11,340
Alright, alright.

70
00:04:20,390 --> 00:04:21,450
Don't cry anymore.

71
00:04:26,630 --> 00:04:28,090
Qiu Agui's death sentence

72
00:04:29,120 --> 00:04:30,650
has already been approved.

73
00:04:32,240 --> 00:04:34,170
It will be carried out in a few days.

74
00:04:41,310 --> 00:04:41,770
Auntie,

75
00:04:44,190 --> 00:04:45,920
could I, when the time comes...

76
00:04:47,360 --> 00:04:48,560
take a message to her?

77
00:04:49,270 --> 00:04:50,730
I'll say that you told me

78
00:04:51,480 --> 00:04:52,740
you'd take good care of

79
00:04:53,310 --> 00:04:54,800
her 3 children.

80
00:04:55,190 --> 00:04:56,250
Would that be okay?

81
00:05:01,120 --> 00:05:01,680
Also,

82
00:05:02,750 --> 00:05:03,910
could you find her

83
00:05:04,040 --> 00:05:05,480
a set of clean clothes?

84
00:05:06,240 --> 00:05:07,500
I'll bring them to her.

85
00:05:08,030 --> 00:05:08,760
After all...

86
00:05:09,240 --> 00:05:10,970
After all, it's all in the past.

87
00:05:11,870 --> 00:05:13,240
You used to be a family,

88
00:05:13,830 --> 00:05:14,360
right?

89
00:05:20,680 --> 00:05:21,140
Auntie,

90
00:05:21,750 --> 00:05:23,750
there's one more thing I want to say.

91
00:05:23,750 --> 00:05:25,080
If I shouldn't say this,

92
00:05:25,800 --> 00:05:27,060
please don't be angry.

93
00:05:30,390 --> 00:05:32,630
Could I tell Qiu Agui that...

94
00:05:35,040 --> 00:05:36,700
you've already forgiven her?

95
00:05:57,600 --> 00:05:59,530
Swiftly and severely crack down on

96
00:05:59,800 --> 00:06:02,270
criminal offenses
in accordance with the law,

97
00:06:02,270 --> 00:06:04,720
effectively maintain
social order and stability,

98
00:06:04,720 --> 00:06:07,040
and ensure
the safety of people's property.

99
00:06:07,040 --> 00:06:07,920
Rapist!

100
00:06:08,430 --> 00:06:09,830
Are you worthy of the people's trust?

101
00:06:09,830 --> 00:06:10,600
You rapist!

102
00:06:10,620 --> 00:06:11,700
You're a teacher!

103
00:06:11,760 --> 00:06:13,160
Are you even worthy of
being a teacher of the people?

104
00:06:13,160 --> 00:06:14,920
You beast in human form!

105
00:06:14,950 --> 00:06:15,480
Trash!

106
00:06:16,560 --> 00:06:17,560
You scumbag!

107
00:06:18,070 --> 00:06:19,310
Immediate execution.

108
00:06:19,310 --> 00:06:20,480
Qiao Zhiliang!

109
00:06:21,560 --> 00:06:22,950
Qiao Zhiliang!

110
00:06:23,430 --> 00:06:25,310
Crack down on criminal offenses,

111
00:06:25,950 --> 00:06:28,310
effectively maintain
social order and stability,

112
00:06:28,310 --> 00:06:30,770
and ensure
the safety of people's property.

113
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:32,400
Criminal Jiang Meiyu...

114
00:06:32,730 --> 00:06:33,970
Qiao Zhiliang!

115
00:06:36,310 --> 00:06:39,360
How am I supposed to
explain this to our kids?

116
00:06:39,750 --> 00:06:41,710
Sentenced to death.

117
00:06:42,159 --> 00:06:43,420
Immediate execution.

118
00:07:42,720 --> 00:07:43,120
I...

119
00:07:45,680 --> 00:07:47,210
think I understand you now.

120
00:07:48,920 --> 00:07:49,920
Understand what?

121
00:07:51,390 --> 00:07:51,990
I'm sorry.

122
00:07:54,680 --> 00:07:56,070
I-I don't know what you're talking about,

123
00:07:56,070 --> 00:07:58,130
but you don't need to apologize to me,

124
00:07:58,390 --> 00:07:59,720
no matter what it's for.

125
00:08:05,750 --> 00:08:06,150
But...

126
00:08:08,510 --> 00:08:09,430
that doesn't mean I think

127
00:08:09,430 --> 00:08:10,800
our choice was right.

128
00:08:17,630 --> 00:08:19,090
I'm not any better either.

129
00:08:20,230 --> 00:08:21,560
I'm even worse than you.

130
00:08:28,270 --> 00:08:29,000
That's it.

131
00:09:01,040 --> 00:09:02,420
[Parading criminals in public was a temporary measure
during the special circumstances]

132
00:09:02,420 --> 00:09:03,810
of the Strike-Hard Campaign,
later explicitly banned.]

133
00:09:06,600 --> 00:09:10,630
[It marked a shift from harsh deterrence
to modern rule-of-law governance]

134
00:09:10,630 --> 00:09:14,660
based on due process
and respect for human dignity.]

135
00:09:23,200 --> 00:09:24,260
You looking for me?

136
00:09:28,910 --> 00:09:29,510
So...

137
00:09:49,550 --> 00:09:50,200
Yingjie!

138
00:09:50,790 --> 00:09:51,360
Yingjie!

139
00:09:53,510 --> 00:09:54,310
What's wrong?

140
00:09:56,000 --> 00:09:57,530
Li Xiang has been arrested.

141
00:10:06,350 --> 00:10:08,480
Yizhong, you have to think it through.

142
00:10:08,510 --> 00:10:10,000
If Li Xiang can be arrested
just for doing his duty,

143
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:11,000
you could be next.

144
00:10:11,600 --> 00:10:13,150
What the hell are you afraid of?

145
00:10:13,150 --> 00:10:13,950
Come what may.

146
00:10:14,120 --> 00:10:15,450
What are you going to do?

147
00:10:17,080 --> 00:10:17,960
I don't know either.

148
00:10:17,960 --> 00:10:19,960
I'll make some preparations first.

149
00:10:21,200 --> 00:10:22,200
Court Pres. Ding,

150
00:10:22,360 --> 00:10:24,200
Lawyer Li Xiang
has been criminally detained.

151
00:10:24,200 --> 00:10:25,600
Didn't you know about this?

152
00:10:25,600 --> 00:10:26,250
I didn't.

153
00:10:26,870 --> 00:10:27,750
He just got detained.

154
00:10:27,750 --> 00:10:28,870
How would I know?

155
00:10:29,510 --> 00:10:31,080
He's nowhere near being tried in court.

156
00:10:31,080 --> 00:10:32,000
Didn't someone

157
00:10:32,020 --> 00:10:33,750
give you a heads-up a long time ago?

158
00:10:33,750 --> 00:10:34,200
So?

159
00:10:36,910 --> 00:10:39,040
Is this a struggle session against me?

160
00:10:39,600 --> 00:10:42,720
I've been forced into the jet-like posture
plenty of times before.

161
00:10:42,720 --> 00:10:43,180
Come on.

162
00:10:43,480 --> 00:10:44,390
Court Pres. Ding, don't be mad.

163
00:10:44,390 --> 00:10:45,790
That's not what we meant.

164
00:10:46,480 --> 00:10:47,460
Besides Li Xiang,

165
00:10:47,460 --> 00:10:48,080
Director Hong

166
00:10:48,080 --> 00:10:48,690
was also detained.

167
00:10:48,690 --> 00:10:49,690
Did you know that?

168
00:10:49,910 --> 00:10:50,440
When?

169
00:10:50,790 --> 00:10:52,520
Don't you have anything to say?

170
00:10:57,390 --> 00:10:58,850
You all can go back for now.

171
00:11:00,550 --> 00:11:01,550
Court Pres. Ding,

172
00:11:01,910 --> 00:11:03,600
Lawyer Li Xiang was appointed

173
00:11:03,630 --> 00:11:05,670
by our court to defend the client.

174
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:09,080
Regardless of whether his views
are right or wrong,

175
00:11:09,080 --> 00:11:10,880
he was only fulfilling his duty.

176
00:11:11,480 --> 00:11:13,150
Therefore, Lawyer Li Xiang's
personal rights

177
00:11:13,150 --> 00:11:13,770
and his right to provide a defense

178
00:11:13,770 --> 00:11:14,970
should be protected.

179
00:11:15,600 --> 00:11:16,720
Otherwise, why would the country

180
00:11:16,720 --> 00:11:18,200
establish the legal profession?

181
00:11:18,200 --> 00:11:19,000
That's right.

182
00:11:22,240 --> 00:11:23,390
But why are you

183
00:11:23,750 --> 00:11:24,680
telling me this?

184
00:11:24,790 --> 00:11:26,120
Actually, we came today

185
00:11:26,890 --> 00:11:27,600
to ask you

186
00:11:27,630 --> 00:11:28,760
to make us a promise—

187
00:11:29,390 --> 00:11:30,320
that on this matter

188
00:11:30,320 --> 00:11:31,870
concerning Lawyer Li Xiang,

189
00:11:31,870 --> 00:11:33,130
you must hold the line.

190
00:11:33,150 --> 00:11:34,960
I haven't seen anything yet.

191
00:11:36,870 --> 00:11:38,420
What am I supposed to promise?

192
00:11:38,420 --> 00:11:39,080
Just because you're

193
00:11:39,080 --> 00:11:40,880
college students from Beijing?

194
00:11:41,600 --> 00:11:43,440
Just because you think you're

195
00:11:43,680 --> 00:11:45,480
standing on the side of justice,

196
00:11:45,670 --> 00:11:46,240
does that mean

197
00:11:46,240 --> 00:11:47,700
I have to go along with you?

198
00:11:47,790 --> 00:11:48,910
You're just stirring up trouble!

199
00:11:48,910 --> 00:11:49,960
Under the leadership of the Party,

200
00:11:49,960 --> 00:11:51,910
the state is vigorously advancing
the development of the legal system.

201
00:11:51,910 --> 00:11:53,770
Improving the system takes time!

202
00:11:54,960 --> 00:11:56,620
You're here on an internship,

203
00:11:56,850 --> 00:11:58,450
not to run this court,

204
00:11:58,480 --> 00:11:59,210
understand?

205
00:12:01,390 --> 00:12:01,840
Leave!

206
00:12:02,480 --> 00:12:03,480
All of you, leave!

207
00:12:03,790 --> 00:12:04,390
Go back.

208
00:12:04,910 --> 00:12:05,480
Go back!

209
00:12:17,510 --> 00:12:18,080
Court Pres. Ding.

210
00:12:18,080 --> 00:12:18,940
Close the door!

211
00:12:21,360 --> 00:12:22,550
Director Hong
from the Legal Advisory Office

212
00:12:22,550 --> 00:12:24,080
and Li Xiang were arrested.

213
00:12:25,200 --> 00:12:25,790
Get lost!

214
00:12:35,550 --> 00:12:36,120
How much?

215
00:12:37,150 --> 00:12:39,410
Seventy-five yuan and sixty-three fen.

216
00:12:39,790 --> 00:12:41,270
Which court sentenced you?

217
00:12:41,270 --> 00:12:42,330
The commune court.

218
00:12:43,030 --> 00:12:44,630
They said I cooked the books.

219
00:12:44,720 --> 00:12:46,390
For 75 yuan and 63 fen—

220
00:12:46,790 --> 00:12:48,150
such an exact amount—

221
00:12:48,750 --> 00:12:50,120
they sentenced me to 2 years.

222
00:12:50,120 --> 00:12:50,550
Wait.

223
00:12:51,960 --> 00:12:53,820
Didn't you say you served 5 years?

224
00:12:56,360 --> 00:12:57,690
I went to prison in 1965.

225
00:12:58,440 --> 00:12:59,500
In 1966, didn't...

226
00:13:00,240 --> 00:13:01,370
the movement start?

227
00:13:01,720 --> 00:13:03,080
Everyone was busy

228
00:13:03,200 --> 00:13:04,750
smashing the police,
prosecutors, and courts

229
00:13:04,750 --> 00:13:05,880
and forgot about me.

230
00:13:06,440 --> 00:13:08,370
So I ended up serving 3 extra years.

231
00:13:08,630 --> 00:13:09,790
1965...

232
00:13:12,790 --> 00:13:14,320
Such an old case.

233
00:13:15,440 --> 00:13:17,570
I've been wronged for nearly 20 years.

234
00:13:18,630 --> 00:13:20,540
You're my last hope.

235
00:13:21,240 --> 00:13:22,630
I've long heard the villagers say

236
00:13:22,630 --> 00:13:24,750
our village has an "Upright Judge Zhang."

237
00:13:24,750 --> 00:13:26,200
Where is the written verdict?

238
00:13:26,200 --> 00:13:29,240
I've never even seen... the verdict.

239
00:13:29,480 --> 00:13:30,270
Impossible.

240
00:13:30,870 --> 00:13:31,670
No matter how chaotic things
were back then,

241
00:13:31,670 --> 00:13:33,530
there had to be a written verdict.

242
00:13:33,630 --> 00:13:35,080
Besides, in 1965,

243
00:13:35,080 --> 00:13:37,270
the legal system
hadn't been destroyed yet.

244
00:13:37,270 --> 00:13:38,720
I-Is that so?

245
00:13:39,270 --> 00:13:40,320
Is that so?

246
00:13:41,680 --> 00:13:42,590
Maybe.

247
00:13:44,030 --> 00:13:44,600
But

248
00:13:45,120 --> 00:13:46,920
I don't know where to look for it.

249
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:48,510
Mentor.

250
00:13:54,710 --> 00:13:55,840
Wait for me a moment.

251
00:13:56,030 --> 00:13:56,870
Have some water

252
00:13:56,870 --> 00:13:57,600
and peanuts.

253
00:13:59,510 --> 00:14:00,200
Mentor,

254
00:14:00,600 --> 00:14:02,340
let's discuss this purely
from a professional perspective.

255
00:14:02,340 --> 00:14:03,600
What do you think we can do

256
00:14:03,600 --> 00:14:04,860
to make Li Xiang's case

257
00:14:04,870 --> 00:14:05,900
more favorable?

258
00:14:10,790 --> 00:14:12,190
I haven't had a chance...

259
00:14:12,950 --> 00:14:14,410
to look into the case file.

260
00:14:15,120 --> 00:14:16,120
And Li Xiang...

261
00:14:16,510 --> 00:14:18,240
I haven't presided over his trial either.

262
00:14:18,240 --> 00:14:18,840
So...

263
00:14:20,080 --> 00:14:21,550
I really can't say much.

264
00:14:23,550 --> 00:14:24,360
But, Mentor,

265
00:14:25,150 --> 00:14:26,030
if all of us choose

266
00:14:26,030 --> 00:14:27,360
to close our eyes,

267
00:14:27,960 --> 00:14:29,360
then China's legal system may not

268
00:14:29,360 --> 00:14:32,030
get back on the right track
for another 100 years.

269
00:14:32,030 --> 00:14:33,030
Why don't we go find

270
00:14:33,030 --> 00:14:34,320
Court Pres. Ding again?

271
00:14:34,320 --> 00:14:34,920
I think...

272
00:14:35,870 --> 00:14:36,720
there's really no point

273
00:14:36,720 --> 00:14:38,790
in you seeing the court president again.

274
00:14:38,790 --> 00:14:40,910
Actually, from a certain perspective,

275
00:14:40,910 --> 00:14:42,440
he's trying to protect you.

276
00:14:43,870 --> 00:14:45,750
Court Pres. Ding is different from me.

277
00:14:45,750 --> 00:14:47,200
He's the head of the court.

278
00:14:47,200 --> 00:14:49,060
Once he says something publicly,

279
00:14:49,440 --> 00:14:50,840
he can't take it back.

280
00:14:51,360 --> 00:14:53,020
So everything he says and does

281
00:14:54,080 --> 00:14:55,480
isn't just about the law—

282
00:14:57,000 --> 00:14:58,200
it's political, too.

283
00:14:58,510 --> 00:15:00,150
Court Pres. Ding will decide
who presides over the case.

284
00:15:00,150 --> 00:15:02,080
I have no way to apply for it myself.

285
00:15:02,510 --> 00:15:03,320
It seems...

286
00:15:04,480 --> 00:15:06,540
they're using Li Xiang as an example.

287
00:15:07,870 --> 00:15:08,330
Mentor,

288
00:15:09,080 --> 00:15:11,080
if we set Li Xiang's case aside
for a moment—

289
00:15:11,080 --> 00:15:12,000
shouldn't we protect the legal profession

290
00:15:12,000 --> 00:15:12,510
that has only just

291
00:15:12,510 --> 00:15:13,640
begun to take shape?

292
00:15:13,720 --> 00:15:14,670
I'd rather believe

293
00:15:14,670 --> 00:15:16,870
that you're trying to protect Li Xiang.

294
00:15:17,750 --> 00:15:18,850
That sounds

295
00:15:19,510 --> 00:15:20,710
a bit more realistic.

296
00:15:21,510 --> 00:15:23,040
We are protecting Li Xiang.

297
00:15:24,910 --> 00:15:25,510
It's hard.

298
00:15:27,030 --> 00:15:27,960
Stay out of this.

299
00:15:29,150 --> 00:15:30,080
If this blows up,

300
00:15:30,840 --> 00:15:32,670
6 months might turn into 2 years.

301
00:15:33,300 --> 00:15:33,750
Mentor,

302
00:15:33,750 --> 00:15:34,910
we only told you this because we believe

303
00:15:34,910 --> 00:15:35,790
you're a good person.

304
00:15:35,790 --> 00:15:36,850
Don't give me that.

305
00:15:37,340 --> 00:15:38,080
Whether I'm a good person or not

306
00:15:38,080 --> 00:15:39,410
isn't for you to decide.

307
00:15:54,220 --> 00:15:55,820
So? What did your mentor say?

308
00:15:59,840 --> 00:16:00,840
I guessed as much.

309
00:16:01,240 --> 00:16:02,030
Whenever something like this happens,

310
00:16:02,030 --> 00:16:03,200
all the so-called idols,

311
00:16:03,200 --> 00:16:04,270
the "upright judges,"
and the old legal pioneers

312
00:16:04,270 --> 00:16:05,600
show their true colors.

313
00:16:06,550 --> 00:16:08,000
Arresting lawyers—

314
00:16:08,320 --> 00:16:09,610
they've really got some nerve.

315
00:16:09,610 --> 00:16:11,120
Things like this happen all the time
at the grassroots level.

316
00:16:11,120 --> 00:16:11,720
It's just that

317
00:16:11,720 --> 00:16:13,120
we happened to run into it.

318
00:16:13,120 --> 00:16:14,550
Well, in a small place like Nanyu,

319
00:16:14,550 --> 00:16:16,070
if a lawyer gets sentenced,

320
00:16:16,070 --> 00:16:17,400
who cares and who knows?

321
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:19,400
Two years in prison
and the person will be ruined.

322
00:16:19,400 --> 00:16:21,200
And there won't even be a ripple.

323
00:16:25,910 --> 00:16:27,040
Where are you going?

324
00:16:33,790 --> 00:16:34,190
Leave!

325
00:16:34,200 --> 00:16:34,640
No.

326
00:16:34,860 --> 00:16:35,360
Hurry, leave!

327
00:16:35,360 --> 00:16:36,560
I have to see Li Xiang.

328
00:16:37,270 --> 00:16:39,440
Who do you think you are,
messing around here?

329
00:16:39,440 --> 00:16:40,960
I have the right to see Li Xiang.

330
00:16:40,960 --> 00:16:41,670
What right do you have?

331
00:16:41,670 --> 00:16:42,750
You're not even a lawyer.

332
00:16:42,750 --> 00:16:44,170
This represents the law.

333
00:16:44,270 --> 00:16:44,960
What law?

334
00:16:45,000 --> 00:16:46,060
Leave, leave, now!

335
00:16:58,480 --> 00:16:59,680
I want to see Li Xiang!

336
00:17:00,200 --> 00:17:01,080
I want to see Li Xiang!

337
00:17:01,080 --> 00:17:02,080
Stop right there!

338
00:17:04,960 --> 00:17:05,829
I have the right to see Li Xiang.

339
00:17:05,829 --> 00:17:06,760
I'm telling you—

340
00:17:06,880 --> 00:17:07,349
if you keep causing trouble here,

341
00:17:07,349 --> 00:17:08,880
you'll be in for it! Hear me?

342
00:17:15,160 --> 00:17:15,920
Why are you

343
00:17:15,920 --> 00:17:16,880
in such a hurry?

344
00:17:17,550 --> 00:17:18,440
The criminal law
and the criminal procedure law

345
00:17:18,440 --> 00:17:19,920
were only enacted
a little over 3 years ago,

346
00:17:19,920 --> 00:17:22,119
and you're proposing a major revision?

347
00:17:22,960 --> 00:17:26,490
The situation in the country is urgent.
We can't afford to wait.

348
00:17:27,640 --> 00:17:28,310
Cheng,

349
00:17:29,400 --> 00:17:31,660
laws are supposed to lag behind reality.

350
00:17:31,720 --> 00:17:32,780
Most importantly,

351
00:17:33,550 --> 00:17:34,960
they need to be stable.

352
00:17:35,880 --> 00:17:37,510
I have no objection to that.

353
00:17:39,510 --> 00:17:40,040
But Zhou,

354
00:17:40,830 --> 00:17:41,830
look at

355
00:17:42,590 --> 00:17:43,850
the recent situation.

356
00:17:44,310 --> 00:17:45,960
Isn't the problem serious?

357
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:49,330
But they're, after all,

358
00:17:49,790 --> 00:17:52,920
China's first criminal law
and criminal procedure law.

359
00:17:54,030 --> 00:17:55,360
When they were drafted,

360
00:17:55,680 --> 00:17:56,880
we had no experience.

361
00:17:57,030 --> 00:17:58,010
Then we need to hurry and fix it—

362
00:17:58,010 --> 00:17:58,960
better late than never.

363
00:17:58,960 --> 00:18:00,360
You make it sound so easy.

364
00:18:00,550 --> 00:18:02,790
Reporting the situation to the higher-ups

365
00:18:02,790 --> 00:18:03,920
has to go through a process.

366
00:18:03,920 --> 00:18:05,920
Then let's move quickly.

367
00:18:10,920 --> 00:18:11,350
Hello?

368
00:18:12,430 --> 00:18:13,430
This is Zhou Yipu.

369
00:18:14,780 --> 00:18:15,620
Xia Yingjie.

370
00:18:15,720 --> 00:18:16,960
How is your internship

371
00:18:16,960 --> 00:18:17,880
in Nanyu going?

372
00:18:20,000 --> 00:18:20,550
What?

373
00:18:22,510 --> 00:18:23,160
Why?

374
00:18:24,660 --> 00:18:25,030
No, when...

375
00:18:25,030 --> 00:18:26,240
when did this happen?

376
00:18:28,200 --> 00:18:29,030
No, no, no!

377
00:18:29,510 --> 00:18:31,370
You must not act rashly right now.

378
00:18:31,440 --> 00:18:32,600
What you need to do now

379
00:18:32,600 --> 00:18:33,350
is organize all the materials

380
00:18:33,350 --> 00:18:34,880
as quickly and thoroughly as possible.

381
00:18:34,880 --> 00:18:36,740
Stay in touch with us at all times.

382
00:18:37,570 --> 00:18:38,550
You have my home phone number

383
00:18:38,550 --> 00:18:39,700
and Mr. Cheng's, right?

384
00:18:39,700 --> 00:18:40,270
Okay.

385
00:18:41,480 --> 00:18:43,210
Take good care of yourself too.

386
00:18:44,880 --> 00:18:45,740
What happened?

387
00:18:50,590 --> 00:18:51,790
Chen Yizhong got arrested.

388
00:18:51,790 --> 00:18:52,480
For what?

389
00:18:54,790 --> 00:18:55,920
A rape-murder case.

390
00:18:57,550 --> 00:18:58,590
Rape and murder?

391
00:18:59,110 --> 00:18:59,910
Chen Yizhong?

392
00:19:00,880 --> 00:19:01,940
It wasn't Yizhong.

393
00:19:04,120 --> 00:19:05,450
The lawyer on this case

394
00:19:05,480 --> 00:19:06,700
wanted to argue a not-guilty defense

395
00:19:06,700 --> 00:19:07,680
for the defendant

396
00:19:07,680 --> 00:19:09,010
and got arrested for it.

397
00:19:09,120 --> 00:19:10,350
Yizhong wanted to defend that lawyer

398
00:19:10,350 --> 00:19:11,350
and argue for his innocence too.

399
00:19:11,350 --> 00:19:12,950
So they arrested him as well.

400
00:19:13,160 --> 00:19:14,740
This is completely absurd!

401
00:19:17,190 --> 00:19:19,450
They actually dare to arrest my student?

402
00:19:24,070 --> 00:19:24,680
Who are you calling?

403
00:19:24,680 --> 00:19:25,240
Zhang.

404
00:19:25,480 --> 00:19:26,810
Why are you calling him?

405
00:19:26,970 --> 00:19:27,920
I'm asking
the Supreme People's Procuratorate

406
00:19:27,920 --> 00:19:28,700
to step in and look into this.

407
00:19:28,700 --> 00:19:29,490
Give me the phone.

408
00:19:29,490 --> 00:19:29,890
You...

409
00:19:32,150 --> 00:19:32,990
Why are you being so rash?

410
00:19:32,990 --> 00:19:33,440
You...

411
00:19:33,680 --> 00:19:35,360
What if the facts turn out different?

412
00:19:35,360 --> 00:19:36,310
If you kick up this big a fuss,

413
00:19:36,310 --> 00:19:37,160
won't that put us in a passive position?

414
00:19:37,160 --> 00:19:38,680
Do you think Yizhong...

415
00:19:38,750 --> 00:19:40,640
Of course I believe Yizhong!

416
00:19:40,920 --> 00:19:44,050
But we still need to
get the facts straight first, right?

417
00:19:47,240 --> 00:19:49,440
Those kids just went for an internship.

418
00:19:49,750 --> 00:19:50,640
Who would've thought

419
00:19:50,640 --> 00:19:52,110
they'd get so deeply involved in

420
00:19:52,110 --> 00:19:52,840
a local case?

421
00:19:52,920 --> 00:19:53,980
Of course they did.

422
00:19:54,070 --> 00:19:55,730
Look whose students they are.

423
00:19:56,960 --> 00:19:57,440
Zhou,

424
00:19:58,110 --> 00:19:59,040
I'm telling you,

425
00:19:59,500 --> 00:20:00,760
I will protect my student no matter what.

426
00:20:00,760 --> 00:20:01,790
Still, we must act according to the law!

427
00:20:01,790 --> 00:20:02,330
I will protect him anyway!

428
00:20:02,330 --> 00:20:04,060
You only know how to talk tough!

429
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:12,200
What did Mr. Zhou say?

430
00:20:12,510 --> 00:20:13,770
He told us to stay calm.

431
00:20:15,320 --> 00:20:16,200
No, what on earth

432
00:20:16,200 --> 00:20:17,460
did Chen Yizhong want?

433
00:20:17,560 --> 00:20:18,440
He's been like this since childhood,

434
00:20:18,440 --> 00:20:18,980
keeping things bottled up,

435
00:20:18,980 --> 00:20:21,000
and when he finally acts,
it's always something big!

436
00:20:21,000 --> 00:20:22,060
I can't believe it.

437
00:20:23,160 --> 00:20:24,110
Where are the two of them?

438
00:20:24,110 --> 00:20:25,970
They went to see Court Pres. Ding.

439
00:20:26,090 --> 00:20:27,400
What's the use of seeing him?

440
00:20:27,400 --> 00:20:28,240
That old fox.

441
00:20:28,720 --> 00:20:30,450
He only cares about his own job.

442
00:20:40,350 --> 00:20:41,350
There's more. Want some?

443
00:20:41,350 --> 00:20:41,810
Yeah.

444
00:20:42,450 --> 00:20:43,160
It's so delicious.

445
00:20:43,160 --> 00:20:44,820
Did you make all of this today?

446
00:20:46,920 --> 00:20:47,960
Slow down.

447
00:20:54,160 --> 00:20:55,000
Why aren't you eating?

448
00:20:55,000 --> 00:20:56,860
I'm not hungry, Court Pres. Ding.

449
00:20:58,330 --> 00:21:00,530
How about we get down to business first?

450
00:21:00,550 --> 00:21:01,150
Business?

451
00:21:02,200 --> 00:21:03,920
I think Li Xiang's matter

452
00:21:03,920 --> 00:21:04,550
can wait until the case

453
00:21:04,550 --> 00:21:05,260
reaches the court.

454
00:21:05,260 --> 00:21:06,420
But you need to do something
about Yizhong.

455
00:21:06,420 --> 00:21:09,150
If he really gets prosecuted,
it will be too late.

456
00:21:10,590 --> 00:21:12,190
I've already looked into it.

457
00:21:12,360 --> 00:21:13,830
Outside the detention center,

458
00:21:13,830 --> 00:21:14,960
he ignored warnings

459
00:21:15,160 --> 00:21:16,760
and insisted on breaking in.

460
00:21:16,830 --> 00:21:17,830
He seriously disrupted

461
00:21:17,830 --> 00:21:18,720
order there.

462
00:21:19,720 --> 00:21:20,320
And he even

463
00:21:20,440 --> 00:21:22,000
shouted radical slogans.

464
00:21:22,400 --> 00:21:24,060
Tell me, wasn't that foolish?

465
00:21:24,440 --> 00:21:26,110
Um, Court Pres. Ding,

466
00:21:26,130 --> 00:21:27,210
if I may interrupt—

467
00:21:27,350 --> 00:21:28,720
this sounds like it could be a frame-up,

468
00:21:28,720 --> 00:21:30,070
or at the very least an exaggeration.

469
00:21:30,070 --> 00:21:31,430
We know Yizhong.

470
00:21:31,640 --> 00:21:33,440
Although he can be stubborn sometimes,

471
00:21:33,440 --> 00:21:34,970
he's not that off the rails.

472
00:21:35,960 --> 00:21:36,590
Of what?

473
00:21:37,110 --> 00:21:38,400
T-T rails.

474
00:21:39,030 --> 00:21:39,830
Off the rails?

475
00:21:42,400 --> 00:21:44,330
I warned you all long ago, didn't I?

476
00:21:45,790 --> 00:21:46,640
This matter

477
00:21:47,440 --> 00:21:49,440
is not something you can influence.

478
00:21:50,400 --> 00:21:51,730
I've gone to the police.

479
00:21:51,920 --> 00:21:53,090
They're very firm.

480
00:21:53,480 --> 00:21:54,810
No one's plea will work.

481
00:21:55,160 --> 00:21:57,000
They insist on handling it strictly.

482
00:21:57,000 --> 00:21:57,960
Don't you see

483
00:21:57,960 --> 00:21:59,420
what's going on right now?

484
00:21:59,960 --> 00:22:01,750
They're looking for model cases
to make examples of.

485
00:22:01,750 --> 00:22:03,950
Then... what do they want to do with him?

486
00:22:04,030 --> 00:22:04,630
What to do?

487
00:22:05,720 --> 00:22:07,970
We'll have to see how it gets classified
further down the line.

488
00:22:07,970 --> 00:22:09,070
With the situation as it stands,

489
00:22:09,070 --> 00:22:10,420
even a detention will follow him for life.

490
00:22:10,420 --> 00:22:12,880
If he's actually convicted,
his life is over.

491
00:22:12,880 --> 00:22:15,140
Please don't scare us, Court Pres. Ding.

492
00:22:15,320 --> 00:22:16,650
Why would I bother

493
00:22:16,680 --> 00:22:18,160
scaring you, kids?

494
00:22:20,350 --> 00:22:22,480
Then whether it's Yizhong or Li Xiang—

495
00:22:22,930 --> 00:22:24,110
even if you really don't want to
get involved,

496
00:22:24,110 --> 00:22:25,180
once their cases reach the court,

497
00:22:25,180 --> 00:22:26,070
you won't be able to avoid it either.

498
00:22:26,070 --> 00:22:26,900
Won't all the pressure

499
00:22:26,900 --> 00:22:28,230
land on you eventually?

500
00:22:37,680 --> 00:22:39,010
So I have to thank you...

501
00:22:40,510 --> 00:22:42,240
for being so considerate of me?

502
00:22:43,750 --> 00:22:44,610
How about this?

503
00:22:46,480 --> 00:22:48,080
I'll do exactly what you ask.

504
00:22:49,440 --> 00:22:50,640
Defy the higher-ups,

505
00:22:50,720 --> 00:22:52,050
stand against the tide—

506
00:22:52,070 --> 00:22:54,160
better to die with honor
than live in disgrace.

507
00:22:54,160 --> 00:22:56,000
If we're going down, we go down together.

508
00:22:56,000 --> 00:22:57,000
How's that sound?

509
00:23:10,510 --> 00:23:11,000
Eat.

510
00:23:13,440 --> 00:23:14,350
Can you handle spicy food?

511
00:23:14,350 --> 00:23:15,750
How about I stir-fry
some red chilies for you?

512
00:23:15,750 --> 00:23:16,230
Sure.

513
00:23:17,000 --> 00:23:18,290
Um, put more meat.

514
00:23:18,680 --> 00:23:19,340
No problem.

515
00:23:33,720 --> 00:23:35,320
Is it really that delicious?

516
00:23:37,200 --> 00:23:37,590
What?

517
00:23:37,880 --> 00:23:39,280
Are we really here to eat?

518
00:23:39,750 --> 00:23:40,550
What's wrong?

519
00:23:40,830 --> 00:23:41,830
What do you think?

520
00:23:42,000 --> 00:23:43,180
Oh, quit it.

521
00:23:43,350 --> 00:23:44,280
What do you know?

522
00:23:44,400 --> 00:23:46,270
This is called "emotional diplomacy."

523
00:23:46,270 --> 00:23:47,030
I praise his daughter

524
00:23:47,030 --> 00:23:48,230
for her good cooking,

525
00:23:48,590 --> 00:23:49,590
and of course her father is happy...

526
00:23:49,590 --> 00:23:50,250
Go on, then.

527
00:23:55,040 --> 00:23:56,600
Diplomacy, my foot.

528
00:23:59,720 --> 00:24:01,580
Court Pres. Ding, we're leaving.

529
00:24:03,510 --> 00:24:03,970
Well...

530
00:24:04,000 --> 00:24:05,460
Well, I'll head out first.

531
00:24:05,830 --> 00:24:06,690
I'll eat later.

532
00:24:06,750 --> 00:24:07,510
D-Don't keep doing this.

533
00:24:07,510 --> 00:24:08,090
No need.

534
00:24:12,070 --> 00:24:13,640
Do you know what crime it is

535
00:24:13,640 --> 00:24:15,640
to forcibly enter a detention center?

536
00:24:15,640 --> 00:24:16,440
What is your relationship

537
00:24:16,440 --> 00:24:17,240
with Li Xiang?

538
00:24:19,640 --> 00:24:20,400
He's my client,

539
00:24:20,400 --> 00:24:22,000
and I'm his defense counsel.

540
00:24:22,200 --> 00:24:23,750
You don't even have a lawyer's license.

541
00:24:23,750 --> 00:24:25,200
What kind of defense are you providing?

542
00:24:25,200 --> 00:24:26,260
Ordinary defense.

543
00:24:29,440 --> 00:24:30,500
Just based on this?

544
00:24:34,270 --> 00:24:35,270
Comrade Li Xiang,

545
00:24:35,830 --> 00:24:38,200
please allow me to provide you
with ordinary defense.

546
00:24:38,200 --> 00:24:39,310
I will do my best

547
00:24:39,550 --> 00:24:42,110
to protect your legal rights
according to the law.

548
00:24:42,110 --> 00:24:42,710
Thank you,

549
00:24:43,160 --> 00:24:44,420
Comrade Chen Yizhong.

550
00:24:47,590 --> 00:24:48,310
I thought it would at least be

551
00:24:48,310 --> 00:24:50,510
a letter written in blood or something.

552
00:24:52,750 --> 00:24:55,150
Seriously, what are you trying to achieve?

553
00:24:56,830 --> 00:24:57,510
A ripple.

554
00:24:59,400 --> 00:25:00,130
What ripple?

555
00:25:04,550 --> 00:25:05,810
You don't understand.

556
00:25:14,160 --> 00:25:15,680
It's connected. Hurry up.

557
00:25:15,750 --> 00:25:16,930
We're getting off work soon.

558
00:25:16,930 --> 00:25:17,510
Okay.

559
00:25:23,440 --> 00:25:23,880
Hello?

560
00:25:24,830 --> 00:25:25,270
Hello,

561
00:25:25,550 --> 00:25:28,150
this is the News Department
of People's Daily.

562
00:25:29,590 --> 00:25:30,140
Hello.

563
00:25:30,400 --> 00:25:32,450
I'm a student at the People's University
of Political Science and Law.

564
00:25:32,450 --> 00:25:33,710
My name is Zhang Lihui.

565
00:25:37,830 --> 00:25:38,430
Forget it.

566
00:25:38,720 --> 00:25:39,780
I'll go back first.

567
00:25:42,960 --> 00:25:43,350
Well.

568
00:25:44,110 --> 00:25:44,570
Mr. Sun.

569
00:25:45,550 --> 00:25:46,790
When the leader gets back,

570
00:25:46,790 --> 00:25:48,400
please tell him about it.

571
00:25:49,110 --> 00:25:49,910
Tell him what?

572
00:25:50,160 --> 00:25:51,590
About Chen Yizhong.

573
00:25:52,750 --> 00:25:54,880
You mean that college student, right?

574
00:25:54,880 --> 00:25:56,410
They arrested him just like that.

575
00:25:56,410 --> 00:25:57,790
If his parents or the university ask,

576
00:25:57,790 --> 00:25:59,270
how am I supposed to explain?

577
00:25:59,270 --> 00:26:00,830
Right now, both internally and externally,

578
00:26:00,830 --> 00:26:02,890
I-I'm the one who has to answer for it.

579
00:26:03,590 --> 00:26:05,450
Court Pres. Ding, have you gone to

580
00:26:05,680 --> 00:26:07,480
see Chief Hao about this matter?

581
00:26:07,480 --> 00:26:08,310
I did.

582
00:26:08,960 --> 00:26:10,200
He sent me to you.

583
00:26:10,410 --> 00:26:11,310
And now, y-y-you,

584
00:26:11,310 --> 00:26:13,170
now you're sending me back to him.

585
00:26:14,310 --> 00:26:16,160
To be honest, I came here today

586
00:26:16,310 --> 00:26:17,440
just to get him back.

587
00:26:17,790 --> 00:26:18,480
That's all.

588
00:26:18,510 --> 00:26:18,960
I know.

589
00:26:19,000 --> 00:26:20,350
You wouldn't actually want me to

590
00:26:20,350 --> 00:26:21,750
take this all the way up
to the Standing Committee, right?

591
00:26:21,750 --> 00:26:22,350
Right, right.

592
00:26:22,350 --> 00:26:24,350
That really wouldn't be necessary.

593
00:26:26,460 --> 00:26:27,160
Actually, the leadership

594
00:26:27,160 --> 00:26:28,510
takes this Chen Yizhong matter

595
00:26:28,510 --> 00:26:29,440
very seriously.

596
00:26:30,110 --> 00:26:32,150
They said we need to dig deeper
into his relationship

597
00:26:32,150 --> 00:26:34,010
with Li Xiang and Hong Zhansheng.

598
00:26:34,200 --> 00:26:35,920
I believe there is a lot more behind this

599
00:26:35,920 --> 00:26:36,980
than meets the eye.

600
00:26:37,920 --> 00:26:39,160
What era are we even in,

601
00:26:39,160 --> 00:26:41,290
and you're still playing these games?

602
00:26:41,790 --> 00:26:43,390
Take care, Court Pres. Ding!

603
00:26:55,550 --> 00:26:56,160
Hurry up!

604
00:26:59,510 --> 00:27:00,510
Court Pres. Ding,

605
00:27:01,110 --> 00:27:02,790
I just feel like something isn't right.

606
00:27:02,790 --> 00:27:03,720
Just spit it out.

607
00:27:03,830 --> 00:27:04,960
I'm quite familiar

608
00:27:04,960 --> 00:27:06,020
with Chen Yizhong.

609
00:27:06,160 --> 00:27:07,690
He's not the reckless type.

610
00:27:08,160 --> 00:27:09,310
Breaking into the detention center

611
00:27:09,310 --> 00:27:10,370
and shouting slogans—

612
00:27:10,370 --> 00:27:12,200
that doesn't sound like something he'd do.

613
00:27:12,200 --> 00:27:13,130
What do you mean?

614
00:27:13,400 --> 00:27:15,000
Because I heard from Yu Gaoyuan

615
00:27:15,000 --> 00:27:16,790
that their family backgrounds
are quite different.

616
00:27:16,790 --> 00:27:18,680
Chen Yizhong comes from
a prestigious family.

617
00:27:18,680 --> 00:27:19,770
What kind of prestigious family?

618
00:27:19,770 --> 00:27:21,300
A family of legal scholars.

619
00:27:21,400 --> 00:27:23,790
Apparently, many people
from Beijing universities,

620
00:27:23,790 --> 00:27:24,920
the SPC, and the SPP

621
00:27:24,920 --> 00:27:26,780
were classmates with his father.

622
00:27:27,110 --> 00:27:29,840
So I've always felt
that something about this...

623
00:27:31,510 --> 00:27:32,920
Go to the public security bureau

624
00:27:32,920 --> 00:27:33,850
to see Chief Hao.

625
00:27:45,240 --> 00:27:45,830
Chen.

626
00:27:49,720 --> 00:27:50,880
This is a comrade from the court.

627
00:27:50,880 --> 00:27:52,010
He's here to see you.

628
00:27:52,070 --> 00:27:52,470
Hello.

629
00:27:52,790 --> 00:27:53,190
Hello.

630
00:27:53,550 --> 00:27:55,480
This is a directive from higher up.

631
00:27:56,240 --> 00:27:57,440
Please wait a moment.

632
00:28:02,030 --> 00:28:02,690
Take a look.

633
00:28:12,160 --> 00:28:14,590
I'm grateful to the leadership
for their trust in me.

634
00:28:14,590 --> 00:28:16,310
The official transfer letter
will arrive soon.

635
00:28:16,310 --> 00:28:16,750
Okay.

636
00:28:18,240 --> 00:28:18,840
By the way,

637
00:28:19,240 --> 00:28:20,110
your wife...

638
00:28:22,270 --> 00:28:24,130
If she returns to Beijing with me,

639
00:28:24,270 --> 00:28:25,070
we'll sort out

640
00:28:25,480 --> 00:28:27,000
of her job ourselves.

641
00:28:27,440 --> 00:28:28,920
We won't trouble the court about it.

642
00:28:28,920 --> 00:28:29,550
Actually,

643
00:28:29,920 --> 00:28:31,070
I'd be very satisfied

644
00:28:31,070 --> 00:28:33,870
if I could just get back to
the Intermediate Court.

645
00:28:33,900 --> 00:28:35,300
But please rest assured,

646
00:28:35,310 --> 00:28:36,650
once I'm at the Supreme People's Court,

647
00:28:36,650 --> 00:28:37,680
I will definitely complete

648
00:28:37,680 --> 00:28:39,110
the tasks
the Party organization assigns me.

649
00:28:39,110 --> 00:28:39,750
I won't let down

650
00:28:39,750 --> 00:28:41,720
the trust
the organization has placed in me.

651
00:28:41,720 --> 00:28:42,050
Okay.

652
00:28:42,550 --> 00:28:43,310
That's all for now.

653
00:28:43,310 --> 00:28:43,640
Okay.

654
00:28:44,030 --> 00:28:44,560
Goodbye.

655
00:28:46,110 --> 00:28:46,640
Goodbye.

656
00:28:55,270 --> 00:28:56,000
Director Du,

657
00:28:56,480 --> 00:28:58,280
I'll get back to work right away.

658
00:28:58,440 --> 00:28:59,370
What's the rush?

659
00:28:59,400 --> 00:28:59,960
What?

660
00:29:01,790 --> 00:29:03,390
You finally made it through?

661
00:29:04,750 --> 00:29:06,010
Going back to Beijing?

662
00:29:06,160 --> 00:29:07,640
I-I'll definitely stand

663
00:29:07,640 --> 00:29:09,240
at my post until the very end.

664
00:29:10,590 --> 00:29:12,440
If you'd been transferred back earlier,

665
00:29:12,440 --> 00:29:13,270
my son might not

666
00:29:13,270 --> 00:29:14,400
have been executed,

667
00:29:15,480 --> 00:29:16,210
right, Chen?

668
00:29:22,030 --> 00:29:23,390
Who is Comrade Chen Fan?

669
00:29:23,960 --> 00:29:24,560
That's me.

670
00:29:26,960 --> 00:29:27,960
We're from Nanyu.

671
00:29:28,270 --> 00:29:30,310
Your son has been taken into custody.

672
00:29:30,310 --> 00:29:32,570
We're here to ask you about some details.

673
00:29:44,110 --> 00:29:44,680
Mr. Chen.

674
00:29:46,480 --> 00:29:48,080
He was talking to me just now.

675
00:30:00,350 --> 00:30:01,590
What kind of statement is this?

676
00:30:01,590 --> 00:30:02,920
It makes no sense at all!

677
00:30:05,200 --> 00:30:05,800
Chief Hao.

678
00:30:07,510 --> 00:30:08,440
Get back to work.

679
00:30:12,680 --> 00:30:13,490
What's the matter?

680
00:30:13,490 --> 00:30:14,620
Why are you so angry?

681
00:30:19,880 --> 00:30:21,590
Is it about Chen Yizhong again?

682
00:30:21,590 --> 00:30:22,310
Hao Junjie,

683
00:30:23,400 --> 00:30:25,530
if you end up taking the blame someday,

684
00:30:26,680 --> 00:30:28,210
don't say I didn't warn you.

685
00:30:31,310 --> 00:30:32,770
Resorting to threats now?

686
00:30:33,640 --> 00:30:35,100
I was just given the order.

687
00:30:35,350 --> 00:30:36,350
I've just sent people

688
00:30:36,350 --> 00:30:37,880
to Jiangyang for a background check.

689
00:30:37,880 --> 00:30:38,790
A background check?

690
00:30:38,790 --> 00:30:39,720
On who this time?

691
00:30:40,350 --> 00:30:41,680
Your student's family.

692
00:30:43,720 --> 00:30:44,510
Hao Junjie,

693
00:30:45,480 --> 00:30:47,140
is it really that big of a case?

694
00:30:48,890 --> 00:30:50,720
Detaining and educating him
for a couple of days is enough.

695
00:30:50,720 --> 00:30:52,980
Is a background check really necessary?

696
00:31:01,590 --> 00:31:03,000
He broke into the detention center

697
00:31:03,000 --> 00:31:04,510
and shouted reactionary slogans!

698
00:31:04,510 --> 00:31:06,480
It requires a full investigation,
no matter where.

699
00:31:06,480 --> 00:31:08,740
He might've been instigated by someone.

700
00:31:10,160 --> 00:31:11,720
He's interning under you.

701
00:31:11,960 --> 00:31:14,960
One way or another,
you'll bear some responsibility.

702
00:31:15,830 --> 00:31:16,890
Trying to scare me?

703
00:31:18,440 --> 00:31:20,040
Can I ask you for a favor then?

704
00:31:22,550 --> 00:31:23,080
Go ahead.

705
00:31:25,400 --> 00:31:26,550
Don't put him together

706
00:31:26,550 --> 00:31:28,010
with criminal offenders.

707
00:31:28,440 --> 00:31:29,640
Don't let him suffer.

708
00:31:33,510 --> 00:31:33,970
Come on.

709
00:31:34,350 --> 00:31:34,920
Get up.

710
00:31:35,400 --> 00:31:36,000
Get up!

711
00:31:36,160 --> 00:31:37,420
-Are you deaf?
-Get up!

712
00:31:38,680 --> 00:31:39,480
Are you mute?

713
00:31:40,510 --> 00:31:41,920
Can't understand simple words, huh?

714
00:31:41,920 --> 00:31:42,750
Can't you hear?

715
00:31:42,750 --> 00:31:43,680
Can't understand what I'm saying, huh?

716
00:31:43,680 --> 00:31:44,920
Get up. Hurry up. Come on.

717
00:31:44,920 --> 00:31:45,550
Get up.

718
00:31:46,200 --> 00:31:47,070
Get up!

719
00:31:47,960 --> 00:31:49,920
Get up. Get up!

720
00:31:49,940 --> 00:31:50,400
Speak!

721
00:31:50,400 --> 00:31:51,160
You think you're tough, huh?

722
00:31:51,160 --> 00:31:52,000
Tough, huh?

723
00:31:55,790 --> 00:31:56,310
Pretend to be dumb, huh?

724
00:31:56,310 --> 00:31:58,370
Can't understand simple words, huh?

725
00:32:02,790 --> 00:32:03,240
Boss!

726
00:32:04,070 --> 00:32:04,750
Let go!

727
00:32:06,510 --> 00:32:07,030
Let go!

728
00:32:07,270 --> 00:32:08,000
Let go of him!

729
00:32:13,350 --> 00:32:14,150
Get off of him!

730
00:32:14,590 --> 00:32:15,830
You'll kill him!

731
00:32:16,790 --> 00:32:17,350
Bro!

732
00:32:31,960 --> 00:32:33,760
You must've fought a lot before.

733
00:32:34,750 --> 00:32:35,950
Never fought before.

734
00:32:36,480 --> 00:32:37,680
I was a model student.

735
00:32:38,310 --> 00:32:40,270
You? A model student?

736
00:32:44,750 --> 00:32:46,610
Would a model student end up here?

737
00:32:47,440 --> 00:32:48,160
Tell us.

738
00:32:49,030 --> 00:32:50,290
How did you get in here?

739
00:32:53,240 --> 00:32:54,570
I tried to make a ripple,

740
00:32:55,440 --> 00:32:56,280
but I failed.

741
00:32:56,750 --> 00:32:58,080
Failed to make a ripple?

742
00:32:58,270 --> 00:32:59,730
And it just fell flat, huh?

743
00:33:17,960 --> 00:33:20,620
So this is how you thought
you could get rid of me?

744
00:33:22,830 --> 00:33:24,720
Don't think your sacrifice is that great.

745
00:33:24,720 --> 00:33:26,480
Worst case, those years of college
will be wasted,

746
00:33:26,480 --> 00:33:27,610
you won't graduate,

747
00:33:27,890 --> 00:33:29,490
and you'll let your dad down.

748
00:33:31,000 --> 00:33:31,480
Me?

749
00:33:32,570 --> 00:33:33,680
I lost my life.

750
00:33:36,040 --> 00:33:37,370
Can you make up for that?

751
00:33:41,030 --> 00:33:42,490
I'm not doing this for you.

752
00:33:42,590 --> 00:33:43,000
What?

753
00:33:43,830 --> 00:33:45,160
I'm doing it for myself.

754
00:33:46,830 --> 00:33:48,200
If I hadn't come in,

755
00:33:49,880 --> 00:33:51,790
then I really wouldn't have
been able to graduate.

756
00:33:51,790 --> 00:33:52,590
Chen Yizhong,

757
00:33:53,640 --> 00:33:54,590
I was only 19.

758
00:33:55,390 --> 00:33:56,630
I was only 19!

759
00:33:58,100 --> 00:33:59,480
Don't even think about getting rid of me.

760
00:33:59,480 --> 00:34:01,610
I'll follow you for the rest of my life!

761
00:34:15,320 --> 00:34:16,000
How do you know

762
00:34:16,000 --> 00:34:17,880
that's what Yizhong was thinking?

763
00:34:17,880 --> 00:34:18,320
I...

764
00:34:19,550 --> 00:34:20,080
guessed.

765
00:34:24,440 --> 00:34:25,150
I think...

766
00:34:26,320 --> 00:34:27,190
maybe it was also because

767
00:34:27,190 --> 00:34:29,050
what I said that day provoked him.

768
00:34:29,280 --> 00:34:30,010
Which one?

769
00:34:30,230 --> 00:34:32,630
I said this happens a lot
at the grassroots level

770
00:34:32,630 --> 00:34:33,190
and that sentencing a lawyer

771
00:34:33,190 --> 00:34:34,790
wouldn't even stir a ripple.

772
00:34:37,280 --> 00:34:38,000
So,

773
00:34:38,150 --> 00:34:40,480
Chen Yizhong wanted to make a huge splash.

774
00:34:42,000 --> 00:34:43,670
But the price is way too high.

775
00:34:44,110 --> 00:34:46,320
If it doesn't work out
and nothing comes of it,

776
00:34:46,320 --> 00:34:47,760
and he gets sent to
re-education through labor,

777
00:34:47,760 --> 00:34:49,670
wouldn't his whole life be ruined?

778
00:34:49,670 --> 00:34:50,110
Fine.

779
00:34:51,800 --> 00:34:53,590
If you don't go to hell, who will, huh?

780
00:34:53,590 --> 00:34:54,760
You're really something.

781
00:34:54,760 --> 00:34:56,190
Didn't you call Zhou Yipu

782
00:34:56,190 --> 00:34:57,590
and Cheng Jianji?

783
00:34:57,760 --> 00:34:59,030
They said they could talk to
the SPC and the SPP,

784
00:34:59,030 --> 00:35:01,030
but there's still been no response.

785
00:35:01,190 --> 00:35:02,510
I believe Mr. Zhou and Mr. Cheng

786
00:35:02,510 --> 00:35:04,440
won't just sit back and do nothing.

787
00:35:05,710 --> 00:35:06,360
So...

788
00:35:07,450 --> 00:35:08,560
I called

789
00:35:08,590 --> 00:35:09,720
the People's Daily.

790
00:35:10,320 --> 00:35:10,890
Really?

791
00:35:11,890 --> 00:35:13,160
Why didn't you tell us?

792
00:35:13,760 --> 00:35:15,630
I was afraid that
if something happened afterward,

793
00:35:15,630 --> 00:35:16,920
you would get dragged into it.

794
00:35:16,920 --> 00:35:18,440
I'll bear the consequences
of my own actions.

795
00:35:18,440 --> 00:35:19,400
You two are really something.

796
00:35:19,400 --> 00:35:20,190
One is bolder

797
00:35:20,190 --> 00:35:21,050
than the other.

798
00:35:21,150 --> 00:35:22,410
You're just gambling.

799
00:35:23,000 --> 00:35:23,610
Will the People's Daily

800
00:35:23,610 --> 00:35:25,540
definitely pay attention to this?

801
00:35:25,670 --> 00:35:27,870
He's just an ordinary college student.

802
00:35:33,710 --> 00:35:34,510
Du Xiaohui.

803
00:35:35,960 --> 00:35:36,320
Who?

804
00:35:38,070 --> 00:35:39,030
I know why Yizhong

805
00:35:39,030 --> 00:35:40,190
did this.

806
00:35:43,800 --> 00:35:44,800
He's such a fool.

807
00:35:46,840 --> 00:35:47,710
Maybe we should make this

808
00:35:47,710 --> 00:35:48,760
even bigger.

809
00:35:50,280 --> 00:35:51,940
Every advancement of a system

810
00:35:52,110 --> 00:35:53,910
requires someone's sacrifice.

811
00:35:55,150 --> 00:35:56,110
No, bro, why do I feel

812
00:35:56,110 --> 00:35:57,150
like you're hoping

813
00:35:57,150 --> 00:35:57,860
Li Xiang gets executed

814
00:35:57,860 --> 00:35:59,990
and Chen Yizhong gets a life sentence?

815
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:00,710
That's not what I mean.

816
00:36:00,710 --> 00:36:01,480
Oh, get out of here.

817
00:36:01,480 --> 00:36:01,960
I can tell that's exactly
what you're thinking.

818
00:36:01,960 --> 00:36:02,920
Stop being so defiant

819
00:36:02,920 --> 00:36:03,480
and dissatisfied with everything.

820
00:36:03,480 --> 00:36:04,590
Why don't you give some real advice?

821
00:36:04,590 --> 00:36:05,720
Fine, fine, you two,

822
00:36:06,150 --> 00:36:07,120
just fight it out.

823
00:36:07,120 --> 00:36:07,920
Fight it out, okay?

824
00:36:07,920 --> 00:36:08,510
See who wins.

825
00:36:08,510 --> 00:36:09,770
Stop arguing, you two.

826
00:36:10,070 --> 00:36:10,670
I think right now,

827
00:36:10,670 --> 00:36:11,780
the most important thing is to

828
00:36:11,780 --> 00:36:12,960
find a way to see Chen Yizhong

829
00:36:12,960 --> 00:36:13,840
and Li Xiang.

830
00:36:14,710 --> 00:36:16,570
What's the point of arguing here?

831
00:36:31,510 --> 00:36:32,030
Wang.

832
00:36:33,280 --> 00:36:34,940
When you become the director,

833
00:36:35,510 --> 00:36:36,840
give me more tasks to do.

834
00:36:37,760 --> 00:36:39,420
I haven't had a case in a while.

835
00:36:39,420 --> 00:36:41,150
Life feels pretty meaningless.

836
00:36:41,150 --> 00:36:42,440
I want to work more.

837
00:36:43,190 --> 00:36:45,120
I promise I'll do whatever you say.

838
00:36:45,590 --> 00:36:46,120
Alright.

839
00:36:47,150 --> 00:36:48,080
In the future...

840
00:36:48,760 --> 00:36:50,070
I'll handle civil cases,

841
00:36:50,070 --> 00:36:51,930
and you'll handle criminal ones.

842
00:36:52,920 --> 00:36:53,720
That's great.

843
00:36:54,630 --> 00:36:56,110
I like criminal cases.

844
00:36:59,030 --> 00:37:00,440
Criminal cases are simple.

845
00:37:00,440 --> 00:37:01,710
First-time offenders,
occasional offenders,

846
00:37:01,710 --> 00:37:02,730
good attitude toward admitting guilt—

847
00:37:02,730 --> 00:37:04,390
even a fool could recite that.

848
00:37:04,920 --> 00:37:05,880
You...

849
00:37:06,320 --> 00:37:06,920
You got it.

850
00:37:08,880 --> 00:37:09,340
Come in!

851
00:37:10,550 --> 00:37:11,480
You never laugh.

852
00:37:12,320 --> 00:37:12,850
Mr. Wang.

853
00:37:14,180 --> 00:37:15,590
Hello, Mr. Wang.

854
00:37:15,930 --> 00:37:16,800
Are you busy?

855
00:37:22,670 --> 00:37:24,280
Busy or not...

856
00:37:24,920 --> 00:37:26,320
depends on what you need.

857
00:37:28,280 --> 00:37:28,810
Mr. Wang,

858
00:37:29,760 --> 00:37:31,280
we sincerely implore you

859
00:37:33,360 --> 00:37:34,760
to be Li Xiang's defense attorney.

860
00:37:34,760 --> 00:37:35,150
Who?

861
00:37:36,480 --> 00:37:37,030
Li Xiang.

862
00:37:39,030 --> 00:37:39,400
No...

863
00:37:39,920 --> 00:37:40,670
Do you know

864
00:37:40,670 --> 00:37:41,800
how he ended up in there?

865
00:37:41,800 --> 00:37:42,360
We don't.

866
00:37:42,840 --> 00:37:44,300
We'd like to hear about it.

867
00:37:48,190 --> 00:37:49,450
Shielding a criminal.

868
00:37:49,800 --> 00:37:50,320
Also

869
00:37:50,550 --> 00:37:51,960
leaking state secrets.

870
00:37:53,510 --> 00:37:56,160
What if, when I meet with him,

871
00:37:56,190 --> 00:37:57,990
he spills all those things to me?

872
00:37:58,320 --> 00:37:59,670
Wouldn't I end up in prison too?

873
00:37:59,670 --> 00:38:00,630
No, that won't do.

874
00:38:00,630 --> 00:38:01,480
I'm scared.

875
00:38:04,150 --> 00:38:05,710
Then could you do us a favor

876
00:38:06,640 --> 00:38:07,630
and take us into the detention center

877
00:38:07,630 --> 00:38:08,490
to see Li Xiang?

878
00:38:09,110 --> 00:38:10,960
Y-You've been colleagues
for so many years,

879
00:38:10,960 --> 00:38:11,360
right?

880
00:38:13,080 --> 00:38:15,140
Let me give you a little legal lesson.

881
00:38:15,760 --> 00:38:17,030
In the People's Republic of China,

882
00:38:17,030 --> 00:38:19,090
anywhere in the country, any lawyer,

883
00:38:19,280 --> 00:38:20,230
as long as they're properly licensed

884
00:38:20,230 --> 00:38:21,400
and recognized by the state,

885
00:38:21,400 --> 00:38:22,630
can take you in.

886
00:38:23,710 --> 00:38:24,570
So this doesn't

887
00:38:24,840 --> 00:38:26,360
have to be me specifically.

888
00:38:26,360 --> 00:38:26,920
And I'm

889
00:38:27,590 --> 00:38:30,120
not as important as
you're making me out to be.

890
00:38:37,000 --> 00:38:38,460
I have a lawyer's license.

891
00:38:39,510 --> 00:38:40,710
I can bring you in.

892
00:38:54,960 --> 00:38:55,560
What is it?

893
00:38:56,800 --> 00:38:58,280
We'd like you to put in a word

894
00:38:58,280 --> 00:38:59,230
with the detention center

895
00:38:59,230 --> 00:39:00,830
so we can go see Li Xiang once.

896
00:39:02,670 --> 00:39:03,710
Didn't I tell you?

897
00:39:05,480 --> 00:39:08,080
Without an official lawyer
accompanying you,

898
00:39:08,110 --> 00:39:09,370
you cannot get inside.

899
00:39:09,480 --> 00:39:11,110
It doesn't matter who puts in a word.

900
00:39:11,110 --> 00:39:11,590
What?

901
00:39:13,160 --> 00:39:14,160
Court Pres. Ding.

902
00:39:17,550 --> 00:39:19,030
Why don't you come in?

903
00:39:22,280 --> 00:39:23,280
Court Pres. Ding,

904
00:39:23,920 --> 00:39:24,780
have you eaten?

905
00:39:30,030 --> 00:39:31,150
So this is the lawyer

906
00:39:31,150 --> 00:39:32,190
you found?

907
00:39:33,030 --> 00:39:33,440
Yes.

908
00:39:33,670 --> 00:39:34,550
I've checked his lawyer's license.

909
00:39:34,550 --> 00:39:35,210
It's valid.

910
00:39:36,400 --> 00:39:36,880
Qin,

911
00:39:37,550 --> 00:39:39,480
the young people are messing around,

912
00:39:39,480 --> 00:39:40,880
and you're joining them?

913
00:39:41,380 --> 00:39:42,530
At your age,

914
00:39:42,590 --> 00:39:44,280
don't you know what's at stake?

915
00:39:44,280 --> 00:39:45,410
Haven't you already

916
00:39:46,190 --> 00:39:48,050
been through enough in your life?

917
00:39:48,320 --> 00:39:49,760
What, you think that's not enough?

918
00:39:49,760 --> 00:39:51,690
You want to go through it all again?

919
00:39:53,480 --> 00:39:54,410
Stand straight.

920
00:39:59,960 --> 00:40:00,480
Qin,

921
00:40:01,150 --> 00:40:02,840
I'm formally asking you now.

922
00:40:03,110 --> 00:40:05,400
Think carefully before you answer me.

923
00:40:06,190 --> 00:40:06,800
Tell me,

924
00:40:07,280 --> 00:40:08,610
what are you doing here?

925
00:40:12,630 --> 00:40:13,030
I'm...

926
00:40:13,920 --> 00:40:15,880
here as Li Xiang's defense lawyer.

927
00:40:17,970 --> 00:40:18,670
Court Pres. Ding, we have a lawyer.

928
00:40:18,670 --> 00:40:19,760
Y-You promised us.

929
00:40:19,960 --> 00:40:21,890
I didn't promise anyone anything!

930
00:40:22,960 --> 00:40:25,420
How many more people
do you want to drag down?

931
00:40:26,590 --> 00:40:27,110
Qin,

932
00:40:28,840 --> 00:40:31,550
there's no turning back
once you take this step.

933
00:40:37,480 --> 00:40:39,920
Thank you for your care, Court Pres. Ding.

934
00:40:54,840 --> 00:40:55,400
Guan,

935
00:40:56,710 --> 00:40:58,710
please contact the detention center

936
00:40:58,710 --> 00:40:59,360
for me.

937
00:41:11,110 --> 00:41:12,510
Have some water, Mr. Qin.

938
00:41:12,840 --> 00:41:14,230
Okay, thank you.

939
00:41:15,760 --> 00:41:17,760
Which school did you graduate from?

940
00:41:22,190 --> 00:41:23,720
It's not worth mentioning.

941
00:41:23,920 --> 00:41:25,180
Not worth mentioning.

942
00:41:25,630 --> 00:41:27,230
Have you handled many cases?

943
00:41:28,150 --> 00:41:30,950
What are you doing?
A political background check?

944
00:41:33,760 --> 00:41:35,160
I've handled quite a few.

945
00:41:38,280 --> 00:41:40,740
No one in Nanyu
was willing to take this case.

946
00:41:40,880 --> 00:41:41,410
Only you.

947
00:41:44,110 --> 00:41:44,510
Right.

948
00:41:47,400 --> 00:41:50,000
For the construction
of China's legal system,

949
00:41:50,360 --> 00:41:52,160
I'm willing to risk everything.

950
00:42:03,150 --> 00:42:03,610
Well...

951
00:42:03,840 --> 00:42:04,710
You brat,

952
00:42:04,880 --> 00:42:06,540
where did you steal this suit?

953
00:42:10,230 --> 00:42:10,760
Li.

954
00:42:11,400 --> 00:42:12,150
Qin?

955
00:42:13,800 --> 00:42:15,600
How did you two end up teaming up?

956
00:42:16,670 --> 00:42:18,470
This is the retainer agreement.

957
00:42:18,510 --> 00:42:19,360
If you agree,

958
00:42:19,440 --> 00:42:20,480
just sign it.

959
00:42:24,670 --> 00:42:25,890
If it weren't for Qin,

960
00:42:25,920 --> 00:42:27,250
I couldn't get in at all,

961
00:42:27,320 --> 00:42:28,030
so I...

962
00:42:46,000 --> 00:42:46,730
Come on, sit.

963
00:42:46,920 --> 00:42:47,920
Sit down and sign.

964
00:42:51,440 --> 00:42:52,000
Mr. Li,

965
00:42:52,320 --> 00:42:54,120
have they interrogated you yet?

966
00:42:54,320 --> 00:42:55,380
What crimes are they accusing you

967
00:42:55,380 --> 00:42:56,400
and Director Hong of committing?

968
00:42:56,400 --> 00:42:58,030
They've questioned me twice.

969
00:42:58,030 --> 00:42:59,960
They're accusing me of
shielding a criminal

970
00:42:59,960 --> 00:43:01,430
and leaking important state secrets.
